          },
          "exactQuote": "In the individual distance events, skaters race in pairs against the clock. Skating counterclockwise around the oval, the skaters change lanes once per lap to equalize the distance covered. The skater in the outside lane has the right-of-way if the two skaters arrive at the crossover point at the same time. Men and women both compete in the",
